      "id": 1,
      "text": "Beaver Dam got its name from the many beaver dams that once held back water on the wash when Mormons crossed the area in 1847.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beaver_Dam%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Henry W. founded Beaver Dam in 1863, originally called Beaver Dams, as settlers established a permanent community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://kids.kiddle.co/Beaver_Dam,_Arizona",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Beaver Dam and neighboring Littlefield are the only Arizona towns that sit directly on Interstate 15.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beaver_Dam%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town’s historic Beaver Dam Station has hosted film crews, including scenes from the 1988 movie On Our Own and the 2002 film Crazy Horse.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beaver_Dam%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Beaver Dam sits along the old Spanish Trail pack‑horse route and later the Mormon Road that linked Salt Lake City to Los Angeles.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
